config.cue (varTrack hosts)bundle.json (acme/schemas)vartrack.json (acme/payments) <pre><code>bundle: {
  platforms: [{github: {
    endpoint:        "https://github.com"
    push_event_name: "push"
    pr_event_name:   "pull_request"
    secret:          {file: "/run/secrets/github-webhook"}
  }}]
  datasources: [{mongo: {endpoint: "mongodb://mongo:27017", database: "vartrack"}}]
  rules: [{
    platform:     "github"
    datasource:   "mongo"
    repositories: ["acme/*"]
    file_name:    "configs/app.yaml"
    branch_map:   {main: "production"}
    self_heal:    true
    force:        {prune: {enabled: false}}   // production never prunes
  }]
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>[
  {
    "platform":   "github",
    "datasource": "mongo",
    "branch_map": {"develop": "staging"},
    "root_key":   "vartrack",
    "self_heal":  false
  }
]
</code></pre> <pre><code>{
  "branch_map": {"release": "production"},
  "prune":      true
}
</code></pre> <p>A push to <code>acme/payments</code> syncs with:</p> Option Value Why <code>repositories</code> <code>["acme/*"]</code> <code>config.cue</code> <code>file_name</code> <code>configs/app.yaml</code> <code>config.cue</code> <code>branch_map</code> <code>{main: production, develop: staging, release: production}</code> merged from all three <code>root_key</code> <code>vartrack</code> <code>bundle.json</code> <code>self_heal</code> <code>true</code> <code>config.cue</code> only — the <code>bundle.json</code> value is dropped with a warning <code>prune</code> <code>{enabled: false}</code> <code>vartrack.json</code> asked for <code>true</code>; <code>force</code> wins connection <code>mongodb://mongo:27017</code>, database <code>vartrack</code> the <code>mongo</code> datasource in <code>config.cue</code>
